Parallel database regression tests
==================================

  timeout 180 ./maxima-local --no-init --lisp=sbcl \
    --batch-string='run_testsuite(tests=[rtest_parallel_database,rtest_parallel,rtest_ask1]);'

Run each configured Lisp. Require the expected test count and "No unexpected
errors" in the log; a zero process status alone is insufficient. These tests
are also appended to the complete suite.

The 20 examples exercise both query engines (kind/propagation and numeric
comparison), exact definite integrals, inherited facts, two different explicit
temporary contexts, errors/throws and LOCAL's normal/error restoration.
Actual workers use separate one-item jobs, so all work cannot silently be
taken by the caller. Threadless Lisps exercise the same serial expectations.

A fixed private generator mixes 512 queries over eight database predicates.
Two workers each insert, compare and collect 96 generated signed rational
numbers, up to 39 digits, using identical seeds to exercise shared numeric
nodes. Expected comparison signs come from exact Common Lisp rational
arithmetic independently of the database's comparison algorithm.

The overlap probes pause each of eight query entry points at BEG or DMARK,
then let a second worker attempt the other query engine. Their shared +LABS
representation differs, and the competitor's CLEAR must not enter while the
first query is paused. A 50ms opportunity window exposes the
old interference: a very delayed competitor can miss the old race, while a
correctly serialized query cannot falsely appear to overlap. The randomized
queries and mathematical checks provide complementary coverage.

A LEARN callback starts database workers: a lock held across the callback
would deadlock. Query fault injection tests both errors and nonlocal throws,
then verifies that another query can use the database again. Helpers restore
replaced functions and join their workers during cleanup; gate deadlines fail
the test instead of letting an abandoned worker wait indefinitely. Run in an
otherwise idle Maxima process, since the overlap/fault helpers temporarily
replace internal functions.

This change retains shared assumption writes. It does not enable automatic
private contexts for parallel runners, or certify unrelated shared symbol
properties and concurrent user-state mutation as safe.
